{"metadata":{"name":"Jami At Tirmidhi","name_native":"Jami At-Tirmidhi","section":{"36":"Chapters On Zuhd"},"section_detail":{"36":{"hadithnumber_first":2304,"hadithnumber_last":2414,"arabicnumber_first":2304,"arabicnumber_last":2414,"name_native":"Chapters On Zuhd"}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":2337,"arabicnumber":2337,"text":"Anas bin Malik narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"If the Son of Adam had a valley of gold, then he would still like to have a second . And nothing fills his mouth but dust, Allah turns to whoever repents","grades":[{"name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}],"reference":{"book":36,"hadith":34}}]}